+# Add t and use it to validate PlaceBlock arguments
+
+## Summary
+
+- Adds the [t](https://github.com/osyrisrblx/t) runtime type checker (`osyrisrblx/t`, pinned to `=3.1.1`, the latest version on Wally) to `pesde.toml`. It's pulled from Wally through pesde like the other packages, and its link is `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t`.
+- `BlockPlacement.server.luau` now checks the PlaceBlock remote's arguments with a t check, `t.tuple(t.string, isPlainVector3)`, instead of the hand-written `typeof` checks. Future remotes can follow the same pattern.
+- Adds t to the package table in `README.md`.
+
+### The handler keeps every check it had
+
+| Check | Before | After |
+|---|---|---|
+| Block type name is a string | `typeof(...) ~= "string"` | `t.string` |
+| Position is a Vector3 | `typeof(...) ~= "Vector3"` | `t.Vector3` inside `isPlainVector3` |
+| Position has no NaN component | `position ~= position` | still `value ~= value`, inside `isPlainVector3` (`t.Vector3` only checks the type, so it would let NaN through) |
+| Block type exists | `BlockTypes.ByName` lookup | unchanged |
+| Rate limit, character and root part, Y >= 0, cell free, reach | unchanged | unchanged |
+
+Bad calls are still dropped without any message, as before.
+
+## Before testing (required)
+
+`pesde.lock` and `roblox_packages/` were **not** updated in this PR, because nothing was installed when it was written. Until you install, `require(ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t)` will fail at runtime and `luau-lsp` will report it as unresolved.
+
+1. From the project root, run `pesde install`. This downloads t, creates `roblox_packages/t`, and updates `pesde.lock`.
+2. **Commit the updated `pesde.lock`** to this branch, so the lockfile matches `pesde.toml`.
+3. Rebuild the sourcemap and rerun the checks:
+   ```sh
+   rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts
+   luau-lsp analyze --platform=roblox --definitions:@roblox=globalTypes.d.luau --sourcemap=sourcemap.json --ignore=**/roblox_packages/** src
+   selene src
+   stylua --check src
+   ```
+   None of these checks have been run on this change yet.
+
+## Test plan
+
+Sync with Rojo, start a Studio play test, and in the client command bar fire `ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock`:
+
+- `("Brick", <a position near the character>)` places a block.
+- `(123, pos)`, `("Brick", "not a vector")`, `("Brick", nil)` and `("Brick", Vector3.new(0/0, 4, 0))` place nothing and raise no server error.
+- `("NotABlock", pos)` places nothing.
+- Rate limit, reach, below-ground and occupied-cell placements are still rejected.
+
+🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
